DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T170000
UID:69c1d0efbfe6da1042250af3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to Canada? Need information on employment\, housing\, lang
 uage learning\, schools\, or other topics? A Settlement Worker can help. D
 rop in to meet our settlement worker every Tuesday afternoon from 2 pm-5 p
 m.\nVisit our branch or contact Ada Tao at 416-770-0312 or atao@cathcrossc
 ultural.org.\nIn partnership with Catholic Crosscultural Services.\nPlease
  bring your immigration documents (PR card) with you
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0efbfe6da1042250af3
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Speed Networking Opportunity for Refugee Professionals
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T200000
UID:6a1ef6ae8ea300e2631a69ae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In collaboration between JumpStart Refugee Talent and Toronto 
 Public Library\, this Speed Networking event introduces refugees and forci
 bly displaced professionals for a series of short\, face-to-face conversat
 ions.\nThese discussions will offer participants an opportunity to explore
  career pathways in Canada\, strengthen their networking skills\, and rece
 ive practical advice on their journey towards meaningful employment in a s
 upportive space.\nSign-in begins at 5:30 pm and the networking event begin
 s at 6 pm.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, First Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1ef6ae8ea300e2631a69ae
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Citizenship Education Circle with CultureLink
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T200000
UID:69de561a4dacf581ff88acda@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with CultureLink\, free weekly sessions to help
  you prepare for the Canadian Citizenship Test:\n•	Learn about the test
 ’s content and structure\n•	Get support and tips from CultureLink’s 
 Volunteer Mentors\n•	Practice with sample quizzes\nContact Rubeen to res
 erve your spot or for more information: rchauhan@culturelink.ca or 437-249
 -7103\nWalk-in participants welcome.
LOCATION:Burrows Hall
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de561a4dacf581ff88acda
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Citizenship Education Circle with CultureLink
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T203000
UID:69c2b756e2a2952aed0a4268@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:CultureLink offers a 10 week session to prepare for the Citize
 nship test. Attend every week to improve your skills.\n- Learn about the t
 est's content and structure\n- Get support and tips from our Volunteer Men
 tors\n- Practice with sample quizzes\nFunded by Immigration\, Refugees and
  Citizenship Canada in Partnership with Toronto Public Library.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 3rd floor\, Discussion Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c2b756e2a2952aed0a4268
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Access to Housing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260624T160000
UID:69a874da4dacf581ff7f9554@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you seeking housing support or have questions about afford
 able housing options? Join us at S. Walter Stewart Library for personalize
 d\, one-on-one assistance with a Housing Services Worker.\nEast York Housi
 ng Help Hub is offering information session on the Rent Geared to Income o
 ptions available in\nMyAccesstoHousingTO\nonline system. Housing staff wil
 l support program participants with hands-on supports and help them comple
 te the registration process.\nFor more information or to register please c
 ontact East York Housing Help Hub at 416 698-9306 or email eyhhc@eyetfrp
 .ca.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a874da4dacf581ff7f9554
X-SOURCE:Volunteer Toronto
END:VEVENT
